From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:48:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Add ext-data-control-v1 support

Implement ext_data_control_manager_v1 for the clipboard and the primary
selection. Data devices get the current selections when they are
created and every change after that, offers can be read from any
selection owner, and sources set through the protocol own the
selection until they are replaced or destroyed. Setting no source
clears the selection.

This lets clipboard managers and password managers, which copy a
password and clear it again a little later, work without being
focused.

Clients in a Flatpak or Snap sandbox don't see the global, so a
sandboxed app can't read or replace the clipboard in the background.
Clients outside a sandbox can already do both through Xwayland.
